      "id": "RLZ-HXT9YW",
      "invariant": "INV-NSG0D4",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-in-tree-selection-adds-rows",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "For a selection whose tree intent says keep, it returns the walk with every family it holds and only records the new intent number, so the selection's answer is folded into the rows already shown. The mounted case \"keeps the first family when j selects a member of the second family only, and k returns\" of `dashboard/src/panels/review/ReviewSurface.walkStore.test.tsx` tests this on the store-authored bodies.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "035768698be6a583041c67e462c149c44d5ba459",
        "content": "sha256:66cab3c39e18f883c05fef12e192c20502ff925d17f267f085ce629679446e8a",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "useWalkedTree"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-QTTT3D",
      "invariant": "INV-BS5PFE",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-keeping-issues-no-request",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Keeps the walk as state derived in the render that shows an answer, never in an effect and never from a request, so no frame draws a tree that lacks the answer on screen and no read is started for the tree.",
      "role": "support"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "035768698be6a583041c67e462c149c44d5ba459",
        "content": "sha256:5c4647aa04bcd595ae27efa2204bcda1061b6bc0a65962538e7df9305d8cdfd8",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "mergeFamilies"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-RKST9H",
      "invariant": "INV-NSG0D4",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-in-tree-selection-adds-rows",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Folds the families of one answer into the families the walk already holds. A family the walk holds and the answer carries is merged side by side, with the change facts united; a family the walk does not hold is added; none is removed. Each family the answer carries is stamped with the subject and the answer it was read for, and the result is sorted by family identifier, so the order of arrival plays no part.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "035768698be6a583041c67e462c149c44d5ba459",
        "content": "sha256:85a6e0153858338536f1bea0e76e9d50da338589ccf9100001c92b0b454a334a",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "mergeSide"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-ZHACZ2",
      "invariant": "INV-MWCCQM",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-kept-partial-family-stop",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Merges two reads of one family side that share the family revision: every member either read returned stays, merged through the roster walk's member merge, and the read that walked further (or, when equal, the newer) gives the page position. The continuation control therefore holds the furthest cursor, whichever read arrived first.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "035768698be6a583041c67e462c149c44d5ba459",
        "content": "sha256:30b4f0708789a9a1253b71abac93875a9cfe1aa77dff295c872a69e4f82430cd",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "rebase"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-ZPH7PP",
      "invariant": "INV-9ZKYWQ",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-other-selections-start-afresh",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "For a selection whose tree intent does not say keep, it replaces the walk at once by one that holds only the families of the answer on screen, and marks it to be replaced by the answer the selection asks for. Another scope (another task context or history view) starts a new walk from the answer on screen. Each intent is applied once, by its number.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    }
  ],
